Review comment:

- [P2] Keep the guard out of switching recovery — /Users/cunxiy/Documents/research/autoresearch-eda/abc-harness/src/map/mapper/mapperMatch.c:91-94
  When `stmap2 -p` is used, the mapper enters `fMappingMode == 4` for switching recovery, but this branch only exempts delay mode (`0`), so the stmap2 fanout guard also skips wide cuts while optimizing switching. That contradicts the new area-recovery-only behavior and can change power-optimized mappings outside the intended modes; limit this path to the area recovery modes instead of all nonzero modes.
